text.section:
The ITAC shall have the power and duty to:

Adopt rules and procedures for the conduct of its business;


Advise the CIO regarding cybersecurity policies, standards, and guidelines, for (i) assessing security risks, (ii) determining appropriate security measures, (iii) performing security audits of government electronic information, (iv) strengthening the Commonwealth's cybersecurity, and (v) protecting against and responding to breaches of information technology security;


Advise the CIO on strategies and priorities for information technology for executive branch agencies;


Advise the CIO on information technology planning and projects;


Advise the CIO on policies, standards, and guidelines for information technology and data of the Commonwealth; and


Advise the CIO on information technology budgeting, investments, and expenditures.
